# DO NOT LET A FORMATTER TOUCH THESE. Not style pedantry — a measured incident.
#
# 2026-08-23: Alt+Shift+F over the docs renumbered the settled-decision list.
# `20.` `21.` `22.` `23.` became `1.` `2.` `3.` `4.`, and every entry after that
# became `1.`, because an ordered list interrupted by prose is several lists to a
# formatter, and each one restarts. Those numbers are cited by number across
# `src/`, `test/` and the notes — CLAUDE.md says "never renumber, only append".
#
# It was invisible to every gate: test, typecheck and build all passed. It was
# caught by reading `git diff`, which is luck rather than a control. So there are
# now two defences and this is the cheaper one:
#
#   1. this file, which stops Prettier reformatting them at all
#   2. `test/docs-integrity.test.ts`, which FAILS if the numbering breaks anyway
#      (proven against the exact damage: 2 tests red)
#
# Defence 2 is the real one, because this file only binds Prettier. If a different
# formatter is in play, the test is what catches it.
#
# Formatting these by hand is fine. Reflowing them mechanically is not.
CLAUDE.md
DECISIONS.md
RELEASE.md
BACKTEST.md
SPEC.html
notes/
